te_observability_runtime_current_authority_build_receipt_v1.json"],"receipt_time_basis":"historical_saved_artifact"},"formal_subclaim_ids":[],"primary_guide_id":"paper_module.agent_route_observability_runtime","primary_guide_ref":"paper_modules/agent_route_observability_runtime.md","registered_runner_ref":"src/microcosm_core/organs/agent_route_observability_runtime.py","replay_id":"replay::agent_route_observability_runtime","requirements_review":{"status":"unrecorded"},"summary":"Checks recorded route events, actor authority and evidence references.","title":"Validate recorded agent routes"},"claim_ceiling":"validates only public recorded route-feedback and observability metadata fixtures, including route-lease consumption, trace attribution, hook-shadow advisory status, anti-pattern debt retirement, behavior-change evidence gates, and public macro body import refs; does not read live operator/provider/browser/HUD/account state, mutate Task Ledger or source, install hooks, certify runtime behavior, authorize pattern assimilation, private-root equivalence, release, publication, or whole-system correctness","claim_ceiling_restated":"Checks the recorded route events, actor permissions, route leases and hook-shadow cases in its fixture trace, and rejects a trace step that has no route lease.","claim_id":"claim::agent_route_observability_runtime","evidence_class":"semantic_validator","evidence_strength_rank":5,"organ_id":"agent_route_observability_runtime","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_import_validation","validator_command":"python -m microcosm_core.organs.agent_route_observability_runtime run --input fixtures/first_wave/agent_route_observability_runtime/input --out receipts/first_wave/agent_route_observability_runtime"},"claim_clause_coverage":{"claim_text_sha256":"5d518adacc55d06ff0a12fa2a9cb5d83b5530b95844fd7cebc666d7b7c231fb6","clauses":[],"mapped_clause_count":null,"status":"unknown","whole_claim_coverage":"unknown"},"classification":{"evidence_class":"semantic_validator","family":"agent_reliability_and_safety","real_substrate_disposition":"real_substrate_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_import_validation"},"component_id":"agent_route_observability_runtime","evidence_state":{"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"fresh_replay":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot"},"guide":{"availability":"available","guide_id":"paper_module.agent_route_observability_runtime","plain":"A log of what an automated assistant did is only useful if its entries are consistent. This component is given a saved bundle of events recorded along an assistant's route, with copies of source files. It checks that no party in the events claims more authority than it was given, that each copied file is the one recorded, and, in a broader run, that claimed behaviour changes cite evidence that can be found. The output is a pass or a list of findings, so someone can see which checks a bundle of records fails.","plain_availability":"available","ref":"paper_modules/agent_route_observability_runtime.md","sha256":"5f3a815e92823f3da4d2759ad02472980c5c5866b0ea17c884ae327e754cb670","text":"# Validate recorded agent routes\n\n> **In plain terms.** A log of what an automated assistant did is only useful if its entries are consistent. This component is given a saved bundle of events recorded along an assistant's route, with copies of source files. It checks that no party in the events claims more authority than it was given, that each copied file is the one recorded, and, in a broader run, that claimed behaviour changes cite evidence that can be found. The output is a pass or a list of findings, so someone can see which checks a bundle of records fails.\n\nThis runtime validates recorded agent observability metadata. The exported example checks recorded route events and whether their actors claim only the authority allowed to them. It also checks source-copy digests and writes a validation result. The broader fixture runner checks trace IDs and references supporting claimed behaviour changes.\n\nThe exported-bundle tests reject a changed source digest. The fixture runner also rejects a behaviour-change claim with an unresolved evidence reference. The validator works on recorded inputs, not a live event tap. A passing result is evidence about these records and checks, not proof that a real agent followed a route or changed its behaviour.\n\n## Run the example\n\nFrom the repository root, with Python 3.11 or newer and the repository dependencies available:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.agent_route_observability_runtime \\\n  validate-observability-bundle \\\n  --input examples/agent_route_observability_runtime/exported_observability_bundle \\\n  --out .microcosm/component-guides/agent_route_observability_runtime/output --card\n```\n\nThe command prints a compact card and writes a validation result under `.microcosm/component-guides/agent_route_observability_runtime/output`, separate from checked-in receipts. A pass reports that this bundle’s checks succeeded; inspect the result for findings if it blocks. The first-wave fixture runner additionally expects a route-compliance bundle at a `microcosm-substrate` sibling path; that layout is not present in every checkout.\n\n## Verification\n\nTests and fixtures exercise the recorded route and authority checks; they do not formally prove the route-observability algorithm. The command above runs directly, without the shared admission gate. `make component-replays` separately runs the exported observability bundle through the [Dafny-verified admission decision](../formal/replay/README.md), checking the host's observations of source and input identities, claim policy and receipt agreement.\n\n## Source\n\n[Implementation](../src/microcosm_core/organs/agent_route_observability_runtime.py) · [example bundle](../examples/agent_route_observability_runtime/exported_observability_bundle/) · [fixture input](../fixtures/first_wave/agent_route_observability_runtime/input/) · [tests](../tests/test_agent_route_observability_runtime.py) · [sample result (historical)](../receipts/first_wave/agent_route_observability_runtime/exported_observability_bundle_validation_result.json) · [JSON record](agent_route_observability_runtime.json).\n"},"proofs":[],"replay":{"command":"make component-replays","command_ref":"scripts/check/check_component_replays.py","command_scope":"all registered components","configuration_refs":["src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#RUNTIME_STEPS","src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#_accepted_organ_runner_module_refs"],"declared_prerequisites":{"availability_status":"not_assessed_by_index","description":"Lean, Swift and test extras required","source_ref":"Makefile"},"execution_status":"not_run_by_index","fresh_receipt_template":".microcosm/component-replays/<run>/agent_route_observability_runtime/exported_observability_bundle_validation_result.json","guide_example":{"command":"PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.agent_route_observability_runtime run --input fixtures/first_wave/agent_route_observability_runtime/input --out receipts/first_wave/agent_route_observability_runtime","expected_result_description":{"status":"unrecorded"},"prerequisites_description":{"see":"paper_modules/agent_route_observability_runtime.md","status":"unrecorded"},"scope":"verbatim historical Atlas example; not an execution request and may target retained receipt paths","source_field":"organs[agent_route_observability_runtime].first_command","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json","usage":"verbatim_source_example_only","writes_retained_receipts":true},"input_mode":"exported_observability_bundle","input_ref":"examples/agent_route_observability_runtime/exported_observability_bundle","last_result":{"artifact_ref":"receipts/first_wave/agent_route_observability_runtime/debt_retirement_receipt.json","artifact_sha256":"819779a6c62749d8